OpenRE-Bench — Data licensing
==============================

This file covers the *data* components of the artifact. Source code is licensed
separately under AGPL-3.0-or-later (see LICENSE / LICENSE.md).

The data in this repository has three distinct provenance classes, licensed
differently.

1. Our curated annotations, metadata, and derived structure — CC BY 4.0
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Everything we authored or computed is released under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This includes:

  - the mined-case provenance and metadata (data/mined_cases_metadata.json),
  - the filtered-pool curation: field selection, per-stage pass/fail markers,
    de-identification, and the selected_into_case flags
    (data/filtered_issue_pool.jsonl and its schema),
  - the mining funnel statistics and filter decisions
    (ingestion/filtered/, ingestion/stats/),
  - the precision-audit sample design and sheets
    (docs/precision_audit_sample.csv),
  - the hand-built case specifications (data/_handbuilt/, the AD/ATM/Library/
    RollCall/Bookkeeping inputs), and
  - all generated experiment outputs (experiment_outputs/, human_eval/).

Attribute to the OpenRE-Bench authors and cite the accompanying paper and the
archived release (CITATION.cff).

2. Original GitHub issue text — rights retained by the original authors
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The mined cases (data/case_studies/<project>_<window>_input.json) and the
filtered issue pool (data/filtered_issue_pool.jsonl) embed text taken verbatim
(after normalization and de-identification) from public GitHub issues. The
copyright in that issue text remains with its original authors and is subject
to GitHub's Terms of Service.

We redistribute this text **for non-commercial research use only**, to make the
benchmark reproducible. To preserve attribution and let readers consult the
canonical source:

  - every issue record retains its source `url` (html_url), and
  - author @-mentions are replaced with `@USER` (de-identification); the raw
    API snapshots under ingestion/snapshots/ are the unmodified provenance.

If you are an issue author and want your content removed or re-attributed,
please open an issue on the repository.

3. Third-party standards and framework descriptions
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
References to ISO/IEC/IEEE 29148, ISO/IEC 25010, KAOS, and the MARE, iReDev, and
QUARE framework concepts remain the intellectual property of their respective
authors and standards bodies; they are used here for interoperability and
comparison, not redistributed as standards text.

